<title>SPAIN: Spain's CNMV cancels suspension Bilbainas.</title>
<headline>Spain's CNMV cancels suspension Bilbainas.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's stock market commission CNMV said on Wednesday it had cancelled the trading suspension of wine producer Bodegas Bilbainas, imposed on June 17, on the Bilbao exchange where it is listed.</p>
<p>The suspension was lifted after the CNMV approved the launch of a takeover bid of Ducde SA, a unit of sparkling wine makers Codorniu, for 100 percent of the shares of Bodegas Bilbainas at a price of 6,000 pesetas each.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
